values ('concepts-1-amino-acids-proteins-2', 'amino-acids-proteins', 'mcq', 'Which amino acid''s side chain forms a ring by bonding back to its own backbone nitrogen, making it a common ''helix breaker''?', null, '["Glycine","Histidine","Proline","Tryptophan"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Proline''s side chain loops back and bonds to its own alpha-amino nitrogen. The resulting rigid ring removes the N–H hydrogen-bond donor and restricts rotation, so proline disrupts alpha helices.', 1, 'MedAi question bank (draft)', null, 'Original MedAi content. Draft, not yet reviewed.')
