values ('concepts-1-gases-solutions-4', 'gases-solutions', 'mcq', 'For silver chloride, Ksp = 1.8 × 10⁻¹⁰. In a mixture where [Ag+] = 1 × 10⁻⁴ M and [Cl−] = 1 × 10⁻⁴ M, what happens?', null, '["Nothing; the solution is unsaturated","AgCl precipitates, because the ion product exceeds Ksp","AgCl precipitates, because the ion sum exceeds Ksp","More AgCl dissolves"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The ion product Q = [Ag+][Cl−] = 1 × 10⁻⁸, which is greater than Ksp (1.8 × 10⁻¹⁰). When Q > Ksp the solution is supersaturated, and solid AgCl forms until Q = Ksp.', 2, 'MedAi question bank (draft)', null, 'Original MedAi content. Draft, not yet reviewed.')
