values ('concepts-1-cars-passages-8', 'cars-passages', 'mcq', 'The phrase ''whom the building is for'' suggests that the disagreement between conservators is ultimately about:', 'When an old building is restored, someone must decide which past to restore it to. A church built in one century, enlarged in the next and damaged in a third carries all three histories in its stones. Stripping it back to its ''original'' form erases the later additions, which may be the parts the community actually remembers and uses. Preserving every layer, on the other hand, can leave a structure that pleases historians and confuses everyone else.

