values ('starter-cars-passages-6', 'cars-passages', 'mcq', 'According to the passage, some eras may really have been more innovative because of:', 'Each generation of listeners seems certain that music was better when they were young. Critics often dismiss this as simple nostalgia, but the explanation may be partly statistical. The songs that survive from any decade are a small, filtered sample: the ones that were good enough, or lucky enough, to keep being played. Listeners compare that curated past with the unfiltered present, where the forgettable majority has not yet been forgotten. The comparison is unfair in a way that no amount of taste can correct. This does not mean that all eras are equal; some periods may genuinely have fostered more innovation, through new instruments, new recording technology, or new audiences. But claims about a golden age should be made with the filter in mind. A fair test would compare the past''s survivors with the present''s future survivors, an experiment we can only finish decades from now.', '["Survivorship bias","New instruments, recording technology, or audiences","Better-trained critics","Fewer songs being released"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The passage names ''new instruments, new recording technology, or new audiences'' as possible real sources of innovation.', 2, 'MedAi question bank (draft)', null, 'Original MedAi content. Draft, not yet reviewed.')
